# The four CI checks, plus the build, before anything is committed.
#
# Same order as the pull request runs them in, cheapest first, so a missing
# semicolon is reported straight away rather than after a bundle. The build is
# here as well because it is the one step CI runs that `npm test` does not
# exercise at all: a renderer that fails to bundle typechecks perfectly — and it
# goes last, being the slowest, so a failing test is not waited on behind it.
#
# Fast enough to sit through. A hook slower than that is a hook people pass
# `--no-verify` to, which is the same as not having one.
npm run format:check
npm run lint
npm test
npm run build
